  "id": "Compound::DB00345 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Aminohippurate and Slc22a11, mediated through the Organic Anion Transport pathway. Aminohippurate binds to Slc22a7 and Slc22a6, both of which participate in Organic Anion Transport, and this transport is linked to Slc22a11. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and moderately strong association, suggesting that Aminohippurate may influence Slc22a11 through the transport of anions. The mechanism appears to involve the binding of Aminohippurate to transporters that facilitate the movement of anions across cellular membranes, with Slc22a11 being a downstream component of this process. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact role of Aminohippurate in modulating Slc22a11 remains to be fully elucidated. The pathways are consistent, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the clinical relevance and specificity of this interaction.",
